{
  "_comment": [
    "Legitimate-publisher corpus for the false-positive measurement.",
    "",
    "Chosen to be hostile to this tool's known weakness: the old detector could",
    "only recognise legitimacy by membership of a 63-domain allowlist, which was",
    "overwhelmingly Anglo-American and European. So this list is deliberately",
    "weighted toward outlets that allowlist does NOT contain - South Asian,",
    "African, Middle Eastern, Latin American, South-East Asian and European",
    "national press, plus independent investigative and academic publishers.",
    "",
    "Inclusion criterion is narrow and checkable: a publisher with a masthead, a",
    "named editorial staff, and a multi-year publishing record. It is NOT a",
    "claim that any of these outlets is unbiased - see docs/SOURCE-LISTS.md.",
    "None of these domains is in ESTABLISHED unless marked allowlisted by the",
    "collector, so almost every one of them has to earn its score from evidence."
  ],
